.TH tkutlgroup n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlgroup
.PP
Group flat rows into a \fBtablelist\fR tree: one parent row per value of a key column, the original rows as its children, with optional sums and a member count in the parent row. Library\-neutral.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutlgroup 0.1
.CE
.PP
Requires \fBTk\fR and \fBtablelist\fR. Uses \fBtclutils::tunum\fR to read formatted numbers (\fB1.234,56\fR) in sum columns when it is on the path.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlgroup::group   tbl rows keyCol ?options?  ;# -> parent keys
::tkutils::tkutlgroup::ungroup tbl                        ;# -> flat rows
.CE
.PP
\fBgroup\fR replaces the rows of the table (\fB\-replace 1\fR, the default); a second call no longer stacks a second set of groups below the first. \fB\-replace 0\fR adds the groups below the rows already there. \fBungroup\fR returns the member rows in display order with the key column filled in again.
.SS Options
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-sum\fR	\fB{}\fR	columns to total in the parent row
\fB\-count\fR	\fB{}\fR	column for the number of members
\fB\-blank\fR	\fB1\fR	leave the key column empty in the child rows
\fB\-format\fR	\fB%.2f\fR	Tcl \fBformat\fR for sums that are not integers
\fB\-font\fR	bold default	font of the parent rows
\fB\-expand\fR	\fB1\fR	\fB0\fR collapses the groups
\fB\-replace\fR	\fB1\fR	remove all rows first; \fB0\fR appends
.TE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tablelist_tile
package require tkutils::tkutlgroup

tablelist::tablelist .t -treecolumn 0 \
    -columns {16 Customer left 12 Article left 6 Qty right 10 Amount right 4 N right}
::tkutils::tkutlgroup::group .t $orders 0 -sum {2 3} -count 4
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Groups appear in the order their keys first occur in \fBrows\fR.
.IP \(bu
Sorting keeps the groups: tablelist sorts the parent rows by their own cells (the sums) and the children inside each parent.
.IP \(bu
Cells in a \fB\-sum\fR column that are no number count as 0.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLGROUP <REASON>}\fR (\fBOPTION\fR, \fBCOLUMN\fR).
